navailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\n\nCurrent plan; retain these exact titles and order, update status only:\n[{\"title\": \"Inspect repository and read words.py\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Implement word_counts in words.py\", \"status\": \"doing\"}, {\"title\": \"Run full test suite and verify\", \"status\": \"todo\"}]\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"finish_plan\",\"next_requirement\":\"Changes and current-file tests are complete. Mark the existing plan done, then final_answer.\",\"remaining_count\":1,\"requests_left\":12,\"baseline_done\":1,\"changed_files\":[\"words.py\"],\"verified_current\":1,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":8,\"max_requests\":20,\"requests_after_response\":12}\nPrevious action excerpt (reference only):\ncontent = '''import unicodedata\n\n\ndef _normalize_word(word):\n    return unicodedata.normalize(\"NFC\", unicodedata.normalize(\"NFC\", word).casefold())\n\n\ndef word_counts(text: str) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"text must be a str\")\n\n    counts = {}\n    current = []\n\n    def flush():\n        if current:\n            word = _normalize_word(\"\".join(current))\n            current.clear()\n            if word:\n                counts[word] = counts.get(word, 0) + 1\n\n    for char in text:\n        kind = unicodedata.category(char)[0]\n        if kind == \"L\" or kind == \"N\":\n            current.append(char)\n        elif kind == \"M\":\n            if current:\n                current.append(char)\n        else:\n            flush()\n    flush()\n\n    return list(counts.items())\n'''\nresult = write_file(path=\"words.py\", content=content, expecte\n[full record remains in run.log]\ncc18b2cb8f80585e710729b2\")\nprint(result)\n\nprint(run_command(argv=[\